/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A fixed turbine has one inlet area.
   - The result is useful boost at 1200 rpm that a fixed turbine sized for rated power cannot reach.
   - A wastegate is a valve that bypasses exhaust around the turbine to cap boost.
   - Compression heats the charge.
   - ε is intercooler effectiveness (0 to 1); T2 is compressor outlet temperature in K; T3 is intercooler outlet temperature in K; Tc,in is cooling air or water inlet temperature in K.
   - Air-to-air intercooler uses ram air through a front-mounted core.
   - Intercooling lowers the charge temperature after the compressor.
   - Supercharging raises cylinder pressure and temperature.
   - For a mild boost below 0.5 bar, many of these changes are skipped.
*/
