/* book exam traps: Do not say the intercooler increases boost pressure. It increases density at the same pressure; the pressure ratio is set by the compressor. | VGT vanes close at low engine speed to speed the gas, and open at high speed. Reversing this gives lag and overboost. | A wastegate and a VGT are not the same. A wastegate bypasses exhaust; a VGT changes nozzle area. | Compressor efficiency is in the denominator of the temperature rise term. A lower efficiency gives a hotter outlet, not a cooler one. | Intercooler effectiveness uses the inlet temperature of the cooling medium (ambient air for an air-to-air core, the cooler loop water for an air-to-water core), not the engine coolant temperature. */
