/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - In a four-stroke engine a separate exhaust stroke removes burnt gas.
   - Burnt gas starts to leave when the exhaust port opens because cylinder pressure is above atmospheric.
   - D is delivery ratio; Vdel is fresh charge delivered per cycle, in cm³; Vs is swept volume, in cm³.
   - ηt = Vtr / Vdel
   - ηt is trapping efficiency; Vtr is fresh charge trapped in the cylinder, in cm³.
   - ηs = Vtr / Vec
   - ηs is scavenging efficiency; Vec is the total cylinder volume at exhaust closure, in cm³.
   - Delivery ratio measures how much charge the blower supplies relative to the swept volume.
   - Cross scavenging uses transfer and exhaust ports on opposite sides.
   - Loop scavenging, often called Schnuerle scavenging, angles two transfer ports toward the back wall.
*/
