/* book exam traps: Delivery ratio, trapping efficiency and scavenging efficiency are three different numbers. Delivered volume is not trapped volume, because part of the fresh charge leaves with the exhaust. | Scavenging efficiency uses the cylinder contents at exhaust closure, not the swept volume, unless the question says the two volumes are equal. | Cross scavenging is not loop scavenging. Cross flow has opposite ports and a straight path, so short-circuiting is high; loop flow uses angled transfer streams that meet and turn around the cylinder wall. | Uniflow does not remove the need for a pressure difference. It still needs a blower or pump to drive fresh charge from the inlet end to the exhaust end. | In a crankcase-scavenged SI engine, short-circuited charge carries fuel and lubricating oil, so the lost charge is not just lost air. */
